# What Vercel must not upload.
#
# vercel.json builds from the repo root and publishes `apps/web` as the
# site root. Anything inside apps/web is therefore served to the public
# web — that is how a mis-dropped upload put a second copy of the whole
# project there, and made the SQL schema, the row-level security
# policies and the Flutter source downloadable from the live site.
#
# Every pattern below is anchored with a leading slash on purpose. In
# gitignore syntax a pattern with no slash matches at any depth, so a
# bare `app.js` would also match apps/web/app.js and un-deploy the
# application itself.

# A second copy of the project, dropped inside the published directory.
/apps/web/apps/
/apps/web/supabase/
/apps/web/test/

# Not part of the site: a local dev server, the developer readme, and a
# duplicate vercel.json that the root one already supersedes.
/apps/web/serve.py
/apps/web/README.md
/apps/web/vercel.json

# Strays left at the repo root by the same upload.
/app.js
/test/
